Subject: MISC: Mass stupidity

> Dale Worley		Dept. of Math., MIT		drw@math.mit.edu
> What I'd like to know, but I've never seen, is *why* the WoD has
> caught on.  Every once in a while there is a big social movement,
> often a very strange and stupid movement, that springs up, presumably
> because there is some sort of meme-ecological niche that's empty, but
> I've never seen an analysis of the forces involved.  In the case of
> the WoD, my guess is that there is some sort of deep-seated fear of
> hedonism in American minds, particularly hedonism when practiced by
> one's children, that it taps into.

My impression is that Americans have always needed an enemy.
After the Puritans escaped persecution in Britain they found
their enemy in witches.  The Colonists later found their enemy
in the Redcoats.  Later we found some excuse to make Mexico
an enemy (and grab a lot of its land).  Then a terrible thing
happened; we lost our external enemies and had to turn on ourselves.
Civil War!

Fortunately, we got to beat up a new enemy (Spain) later in the
19th century and then got to fight the Germans (twice!) plus Japan,
followed by a Cold War against the Russian Commies in the 20th century.
But then a terrible thing happened; the Soviet Union collapsed and
we lost our favorite external enemy and had to turn on ourselves.
War On Drugs!

What we really need is a bigger and better enemy.  Bush started
training Saddam Hussein for that role, but I don't know if
Saddam is quite up to it.  Are there any other takers?

